{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeMarkov3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeMarkov3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRep","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_markov_σ0σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_markov_σ0σ1","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L205-L216","doc":"**Top-level Markov relation for `σ₀σ₁`**: `tr_M(σ₀σ₁) = z · tr_M(σ₀)`.  This is\nthe recursive Markov property `tr_M(σ₀·σ₁) = z·tr_M(σ₀)` with `x = σ₀ ∈ H_2`,\nPROVED as a field identity for the canonical weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_markov_σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_markov_σ1","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L192-L203","doc":"**Top-level Markov relation for `σ₁`**: `tr_M(σ₁) = z · tr_M(1)`.  This is the\nrecursive Markov property `tr_M(1·σ₁) = z·tr_M(1)`, PROVED as a field identity\nfor the canonical weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_σ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_σ0","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L181-L190","doc":"**`tr_M(σ₀) = z`** for the canonical weights (derive-then-check): the Markov\nproperty one level down, `tr_M(σ₀) = z·tr_M(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeights_one","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L171-L179","doc":"**Normalisation** (derive-then-check): the canonical weights give `tr_M(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight2","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L167-L169","doc":"Canonical Markov weight `w_{(2,1)} = w₂` of the `2`-dimensional block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight1","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L163-L165","doc":"Canonical Markov weight `w_{(1³)} = w₁` of the sign block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovWeight0","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L158-L161","doc":"Canonical Markov weight `w_{(3)} = w₀` of the trivial block, as a rational\nfunction of the substrate modulus `q` and the Markov parameter `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ0σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ0σ1","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L114-L122","doc":"The Markov trace on the length-two element `σ₀σ₁`:\n`tr_M(σ₀σ₁) = w₀ q² + w₁ q⁻² - w₂` (from `χ_{(3)}(σ₀σ₁) = q²`,\n`χ_{(1³)}(σ₀σ₁) = q⁻²`, `χ_{(2,1)}(σ₀σ₁) = -1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ1","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L109-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_σ0","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L102-L107","doc":"The Markov trace on a single generator: `tr_M(σ_i) = w₀ q - w₁ q⁻¹ + w₂ (q - q⁻¹)`\n(the same for `σ₀` and `σ₁` — isospectrality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ0σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ0σ1","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L89-L100","doc":"The `(2,1)` character of the length-2 element `σ₀σ₁`: `χ_{(2,1)}(σ₀σ₁) = tr(S0·S1) = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ1","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L76-L87","doc":"The `(2,1)` character of `σ₁`: `χ_{(2,1)}(σ₁) = tr(S1) = q - q⁻¹`.  (The two\nseminormal generators are isospectral: same trace `q - q⁻¹`, same determinant `-1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.char21_σ0","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L69-L74","doc":"The `(2,1)` character of `σ₀`: `χ_{(2,1)}(σ₀) = tr(S0) = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L62-L67","doc":"**Value at the identity**: `tr_M(1) = Σ_λ w_λ d_λ = w₀ + w₁ + 2 w₂`\n(`d_{(3)} = d_{(1³)} = 1`, `d_{(2,1)} = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**Trace property**: `markovTrace3` is a class function, `tr_M(x·y) = tr_M(y·x)`.\nEach summand is the character of a representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.markovTrace3","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeMarkov3.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The **weighted-character (Markov) trace** on `H_3(q)`: the block-weighted sum of\nthe three irreducible characters (trivial, sign, and the `(2,1)` seminormal). ","signatureChunk":0}]}